# chorus golden vector: secure record (the endpoint's first), protocol v2 message type 0x24.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in secure_record.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.
# Test-only keys (the four X25519 secrets in the .fields file) are public: never use them
# for a real device. The Noise prologue is the 7 bytes of handshake_init before the Noise
# message: 43 48 52 53 00 02 01. Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 (noiseprotocol.org, rev 34).

# frame header: type 0x24, payload length 75 (0x004B), big-endian
24 00 4B

# ciphertext: the endpoint's first record after the handshake above, nonce 0, sealed with the first Split() key; associated data is this frame's own 3-byte header. It carries the hello_endpoint frame then the capabilities frame
2B 82 50 CC 9B 9A CF 46 F0 4B 55 1F FB 72 DB 29
1F 99 FE 86 2C 7B 62 4F 32 CF 97 A1 8D A3 E3 26
9F 57 CF 29 2F 51 1A C1 49 2D F8 90 20 B3 E3 75
16 49 CE 96 A2 80 DB 3D 5E 13 80

# the 16-byte ChaCha20-Poly1305 tag
F8 C0 ED 96 DE 4D 23 5B 6A 61 04 FD 4A E6 13 7B
